```c
timeout = nf_flowtable_time_stamp + flow_offload_get_timeout(flow);
WRITE_ONCE(flow->timeout, timeout);
```
Reason:
The code attempts to update the flow's timeout immediately after a failure without any delay or limit, causing the system to repeatedly try to offload the flow as quickly as possible, which results in excessive system load.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (timeout - READ_ONCE(flow->timeout) > HZ)
    WRITE_ONCE(flow->timeout, timeout);
else
    return;
```
Reason:
The fix introduces a condition that checks if the time since the last timeout update exceeds one second (defined by `HZ`). This throttles the retry attempts for hardware offloading, ensuring that updates only occur once per second, thereby reducing system load.

